  "difficulty_level": "H1",
  "difficulty_reason": "The given complex may consist of arbitrary quasi-coherent modules and the scheme need not be Noetherian or have an ample line bundle. The author constructs a global finite-vector-bundle complex by selecting finite-type cycle submodules, resolving them through the resolution property, and reducing the Tor-amplitude through a cone induction. This is a global strictification construction beyond ordinary local projective-resolution calculations.",
